# .gitignore — files deliberately kept out of version control.
#
# Owns the repository's exclusion rules. Grouped by reason so an addition lands in the
# right place. The one non-obvious rule is the `.env.example` negation below.

# --- Dependencies (reinstallable from package-lock.json) ---
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# --- Build output and framework caches ---
/.next/
/out/
/build
/dist
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
.swc/
.turbo/
.vercel

# --- Secrets ---
# Every dotenv file is excluded...
.env
.env*.local
.env.development
.env.production
.env.test
# ...except the committed placeholder template. This negation MUST come after the
# patterns above, because in gitignore the last matching rule wins. Moving it up would
# silently stop tracking .env.example.
!.env.example

# --- Test and coverage artifacts ---
/coverage
# Playwright output. `playwright-report/` is the HTML report (CI uploads it as an
# artifact on failure), `test-results/` holds traces, screenshots, and videos from failed
# runs, and `.playwright/` is scratch state. All three are regenerated per run and can be
# large — traces especially — so none of them belongs in history.
/playwright-report/
/test-results/
/.playwright/
# Browser binaries, if PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH is ever pointed inside the repo (some CI
# cache setups do this). ~100MB per browser; never commit.
/ms-playwright/
/.cache/ms-playwright/

# --- Logs ---
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.log

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
*.pem

# --- Source assets (not the web-sized derivatives) ---
# The photographer's originals, dropped in by the actor: multi-megabyte full-resolution
# camera files. They are inputs to the build of an asset, not the asset, and a repo is the
# wrong place for them. What ships is the downscaled derivative committed under
# `public/images/` — e.g. `public/images/headshot.jpg` (1024x1536, ~344KB) is a downscale
# of `pictures/Ethan4.JPEG` (3448x5168, 2.8MB). Keep the original here so it can be
# re-derived at another size; never commit it.
/pictures/

# Crop candidates generated while choosing the headshot framing (2026-09-25). Kept out of
# the repo for the same reason as the source photo above: they are working files, and the
# chosen crop already lives at public/images/headshot.jpg.
/pictures/crops/
